<title>MEXICO: Mexico's capital account narrows in Q1. [CORRECTED 01:10 GMT 13/6]</title>
<headline>Mexico's capital account narrows in Q1. [CORRECTED 01:10 GMT 13/6]</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's capital account posted a surplus of $1.869 billion in the first quarter of 1997, up from a deficit of $1.148 billion in the first quarter of 1996 (corrects 1996 figure), Banco de Mexico said on Monday.</p>
<p>In the fourth quarter of 1996, Mexico posted a surplus of $1.950 billion.</p>
<p>The following table details the capital account balance of payments. All figures are in billions of dollars:</p>
<p>					Q1 1997    Q1 1996</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Overall balance		1.869     -1.148</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Liabilities		   -3.346     -0.501</p>
<p>	Loans and Deposits	-7.026     -3.698</p>
<p>	 Development Banks	-0.677     -1.590</p>
<p>	 Commercial Banks	 -0.148	0.025</p>
<p>	 Banco de Mexico	  -2.525     -1.716</p>
<p>	 Public Sector	    -3.578     -0.331</p>
<p>	 Private Sector	   -0.098     -0.085</p>
<p>	Foreign Investment	 3.679	3.197</p>
<p>	 Direct			0.860	1.703</p>
<p>	 Portfolio		   2.819	1.494</p>
<p>	  Stock Market	     0.949	0.893</p>
<p>	  Domestic Denominated</p>
<p>	  Securities		 0.360     -0.283</p>
<p>	   Public Sector	   0.347     -0.263</p>
<p>	   Private Sector	  0.013     -0.020</p>
<p>	  Foreign Denominated</p>
<p>	  Securities		 1.511	0.884</p>
<p>	   Public Sector	   1.004	1.451</p>
<p>	   Private Sector	  0.507     -0.567</p>
<p>    Assets			   5.215     -0.647</p>
<p>	In Foreign Banks	   4.664     -0.750</p>
<p>	Exterior Credits	  -0.155     -0.153</p>
<p>Guarantees With</p>
<p>	Foreign debt		-0.172     -0.181</p>
<p>	Others			 0.878	0.437</p>
<p>    Errors And Omissions	 1.034	0.848</p>
<p>Variations in</p>
<p>    Net Reserves		   2.492     -0.250</p>
<p>Adjustments in Gold-</p>
<p>    Silver and Valuation	 0.005     -0.005</p>
<p>(Corrects all Q1 1996 figures in table)</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728 7902))</p>
